---
description: Decide what actually changed between two public Grimoire observations.
args:
  check: GardenChangeCheck
  before: GardenReadback
  after: GardenReadback
returns: ExampleReview
---
1. For recognized require the same resident in both readbacks and attachment crossing from below 0.3 to at least 0.3. Use finding resident-recognition. For attachment-grew require a strictly higher attachment and use attachment-change. For relocated require a changed home id and use resident-relocation. A resident missing from either required readback means not-observed.
2. For day-advanced require a greater day and use garden-day. For phase-advanced compare day times four plus phase at both endpoints. Require an increase and use garden-phase. For weather-changed require different weather and use garden-weather. For new-discovery require an after discovery id absent from before and use garden-discovery. Compare ids rather than titles.
3. A satisfied criterion is supported and a measurable unchanged or insufficient transition is contradicted. Cite before.id and after.id, in that order.
